WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.330
Speaker 1: My friends, once arrested and twice
impeached, failed.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.759
Former President Donald Trump is about to
get arrested again, and this time it appears

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:13.640
federal charges are coming.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:19.260
Trump's lawyers meeting with the Justice Department
yesterday, reportedly begging them, please.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.310
Speaker 2: Please.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.150
Speaker 1: With tears in their eyes, don't
charge Donald Trump.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:31.100
CBS News reports Trump attorneys meet with
special counsel at Justice Department amid

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.399
Documents Investigation.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.079
Great report by Robert Costa and others.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:42.411
Attorneys representing Trump met with special
counsel Jack Smith and prosecutors at the

00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:46.840
Justice Department 10 a.m. yesterday, according
to two people familiar with the matter.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.130
This took place weeks after Trump's lawyers
requested a meeting with top federal law enforcement

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.130
officials.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:57.410
The attorneys for Trump spent just under 2
hours inside the main justice building and

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.070
declined to comment as they left.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.090
CBS News cameras captured Trump's legal team
walking in.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.040
The former president's lawyers did not speak
as they entered a person familiar with the

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.690
meeting between the three attorneys and the
department said Merrick Garland was not there.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:18.200
Two people familiar with the probe say Trump's
legal team is frustrated with how the Justice

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.290
Department has handled attorney client matters
in recent months and would likely raise concerns

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.799
during the meeting.

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:32.200
In particular, prosecutors discussions of
related issues in front of the grand jury.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.060
Additional reporting from The Washington Post.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:43.060
Trump lawyers Ask Justice Department not to
charge Trump in the classified documents case.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.240
We now have reporting here about the reason
for the visit.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.930
Quote, Attorneys for Donald Trump went to
the Justice Department Monday to make their

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.930
case.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:57.780
The government should not charge the former
president in connection with his possession

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:03.490
of classified documents after leaving office,
as reported already in the other article.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.520
They were there for 2 hours.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.960
Merrick Garland wasn't there.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.970
Justice Department has not commented.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.840
This is an interesting paragraph.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.910
While it is not uncommon in high profile cases
for defense lawyers to get such a meeting

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:19.209
with Justice Department officials towards
the end of an investigation, current and former

00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:26.239
officials say such presentations rarely change
prosecutors minds to Trump.

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:31.220
Advisers briefed on Monday's meetings say
they continue to believe Smith will finalize

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.730
a charging decision in coming weeks.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.780
The advisers say they are preparing for a
potential indictment of the former president.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.220
The meeting did not change their expectations.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:50.099
Donald Trump, by all reasonable reports, is
about to get arrested again, indicted again,

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:53.180
this time on federal charges.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.500
These aren't even the only federal charges
Trump might be charged for.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.370
Remember that there is a federal investigation
into Trump's mishandling of classified documents,

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.270
which we now know took place not only at Mar
a Lago, but also at Bedminster.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:11.650
We now know Trump knew they were classified
based on an audio recording of Trump saying,

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.040
I have a document here, but I can't show it
to you because it's classified.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.069
Which confirms Trump knew he had not actually
declassified the documents.

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:23.900
That's one slate of federal charges that could
be coming.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:30.299
In addition, there are the potential charges
referred to the Justice Department by the

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:37.980
former House committee investigating the insurrectionist
Trump riots of January six, 2021.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.330
That could lead to charges.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:44.390
And in addition to that, Fannie Willis in
Georgia will be making a charging decision

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:50.610
on state level charges against Trump sometime
between July and September, when the next

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.340
grand jury is reconvened and those decisions
are going to be made.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:03.849
We could see one, two or even three additional
arrests of the once arrested, twice impeached

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:06.790
former president just over the summer.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.860
The question we are all now asking is whether
this will impact Trump, Trump's campaign for

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:18.049
the Republican candidacy and who of the other
people running for the Republican candidacy

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:20.959
for the Republican nomination stand to benefit
the most?

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:24.900
It seems it's DeSantis because he's the only
one in double digits at this point in terms

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.000
of the polling.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.699
But we'll look at that a little more deeply,
probably Thursday, if not Friday.

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:35.870
In the meantime, Trump's reaction to news
that he will likely be arrested completely

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.300
and totally unhinged

